==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fro|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|divisibilis}}, from the verb {{m|la|divido|}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|[dɪˈvɪzɪbəɫ]|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Capable of being [[divide]]d or split.
# {{label|en|arithmetic}} Of an [[integer]], that, when [[divide]]d by another integer, leaves no [[remainder]].
#: ''12 is '''divisible''' by 3.''

